 "literal": "In deep water, conquers the crocodile; will destroy [it], from the water if [it] departs, other [creatures].",
 "translation": "In deep water, a crocodile conquers all; but if it leaves the water, other creatures will easily destroy it.",
 "modern": "ஆழமான நீரில் இருக்கும்போது முதலை மற்ற விலங்குகளை வெல்லும்; ஆனால் அது அந்நீரை விட்டு வெளியேறினால், பிற எளிய விலங்குகளும் அதனை வென்று அழித்துவிடும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet highlights the supreme importance of choosing the right place for action. A crocodile is an unmatched predator when it remains in deep water, where its natural environment gives it absolute strength. However, if it leaves its watery domain, it loses its advantage and can be easily defeated even by otherwise weaker creatures. This analogy teaches that even the most powerful individuals can be easily overcome if they step out of their sphere of strength or act in an unfavorable environment.",
